\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Measured network-layer performance per routing mode and scenario, averaged across surviving failure-process, fleet-size, and seed combinations. PDR is packet delivery ratio; delay is mean end-to-end delay in milliseconds. $n$ is the number of surviving cell-seed runs contributing to each row; the Philippines scenario uses the full area footprint, while the Indonesia and Vietnam scenarios use larger areas that trigger the ns-3 crash described above more often and therefore rest on fewer surviving seeds.}}{18}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:netresults}{{4}{18}{Measured network-layer performance per routing mode and scenario, averaged across surviving failure-process, fleet-size, and seed combinations. PDR is packet delivery ratio; delay is mean end-to-end delay in milliseconds. $n$ is the number of surviving cell-seed runs contributing to each row; the Philippines scenario uses the full area footprint, while the Indonesia and Vietnam scenarios use larger areas that trigger the ns-3 crash described above more often and therefore rest on fewer surviving seeds}{table.caption.6}{}}
